            <div xml:id="d752">

                <pb facs="0701" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.51/71: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-21T22:00:00+03:06">April 21, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 22—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>118. My 114, April 18, 5 p.m. While Jordan was in King’s camp King repeated
                    request for written statement of intended British aid to Saudi Arabia and said
                    if adequate assistance could not be had from British he would appeal to oil
                    company or American Government.</p>
                <p>Jordan was unable to give desired statement but promised to secure data in Cairo
                    and to answer when he and General Paget visit King at Riyadh about April 26.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
